The stairway has three risers, each 8 inches high, and three treads, each 10 inches deep. The side panel of the stairway is a composite figure. The perimeter along the side panel will be the sum of the heights of the risers and the depths of the treads. Since there are three risers and three treads, the total height is $3 \times 8 = 24$ inches, and the total depth is $3 \times 10 = 30$ inches. The side panel is a rectangle with height 24 inches and width 30 inches. Therefore, the area of the side panel is $24 \times 30$.

$24 \times 30 = 24 \times 3 \times 10 = 72 \times 10 = 720$

The area of the side panel is 720 square inches.

\boxed{720 \text{ square inches}} 
